# Hoop, there it is! 

Imagine you are practicing your free throw shot.

**Round 1:**
You take exactly five free throws.

**Round 2:**
You keep tossing the basketball until you make one shot, no matter how many tries it takes.

**Which round do you think would take longer and why?**



<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px; width:60%;">
    <summary style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">🔎 Check your thinking:</summary>
<div style="margin: 20px;">
    <p style = "font-size: 12pt;">
    <ul>
    <li style = "font-size: 12pt;">In one case, you already know how many times you’ll repeat the action.</li>
    <li style = "font-size: 12pt;">In the other, you don’t know how many tries it will take—you stop only when a condition is met.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style = "font-size: 12pt;"> This same distinction shows up in programming.</p>

</p>
</div>
</details>

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## Types of Loops

Not all loops repeat in the same way. What makes loops different is how the repetition is controlled.

In most programs, iteration falls into one of two common categories.

<div style="
  display: flex;
  gap: 20px;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: stretch;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
">

  <!-- Count-Controlled Iteration Card -->
  <div style="
    background-color: #F5F7F8;
    color: #000000;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    width: 300px;
    text-align: left;
  ">

<p style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0; ">
      Count-Controlled Iteration<br>(For Loop)
    </p>

<ul style="
  list-style-position: outside; padding-left: 16px; margin: 12px 0 0 0;">


<li style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;  padding-left: 0;
">
        Repeats a set of steps a <strong>specific number of times</strong>
      </li>

<li style="  font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0;">
        The number of repetitions is known before the loop starts
      </li>

 <li style="  font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0; font-style: italic;">
         “How many times should this happen?”
      </li>

 </ul>

  </div>

  <!-- Condition-Controlled Iteration Card -->
  <div style="
    background-color: #F5F7F8;
    color: #000000;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    width: 300px;
    text-align: left;
  ">

 <p style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;">
      Condition-Controlled Iteration<br>(While Loop)
    </p>

<ul style="
  list-style-position: outside; padding-left: 12px; margin: 12px 0 0 0;">

<li style="  font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0;">
        Repeats a set of steps <strong>as long as a condition is true</strong>
      </li>

 <li style="  font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0;">
        The number of repetitions is not known ahead of time
      </li>

 <li style="  font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0; font-style: italic;">
         “When should this stop?”
      </li>

</ul>

  </div>

</div>


